<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Let's Take A Sentimental Journey (Don't Forget To Bleed)</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Six year old Catra Leandros has just lost her parents, inherited a metric fuckton of ghosts/psychological trauma, discovered herself through music and fought hard to be accepted into the Right Zone Academy of Arts. And if there's one thing she's learned from the experience, it's that when life seems to stop kicking you in the teeth, it's probably just gearing up to gut punch you instead. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Still, she wasn't expecting that some of the echoes inside her head wouldn't just stay there. Or that the dream girl she's been following around for months is apparently flesh and blood too, along with her nightmares.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;---------&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A series of chapters exploring Catra and Adora's time together at (F)Right Zone Academy of Arts, and how the more things change, the more some things stay the same.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>MalachiWalker</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Mature</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora/Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Shadow Weaver | Light Spinner (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>We're in the fright zone now so you know what that means:</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Shadow Weaver's A+ Parenting</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>I give Catra a happy childhood for five seconds just to take it away</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Because needs be and I'm a MONSTER</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Original Magicat characters because canon hasn't given us any yet</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>And the 80s show had all of four</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>And they all had stupid names</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Tao is named after one but he's basically an OC</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Pretty graphic depiction of a car wreck</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra grapples with her canon self's PTSD transcending universes</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>As if she didn't have enough to deal with</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Coping with emotional trauma by getting really hardcore about your hobby</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Just like an anime character</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>How many times will I recreate The Promise?</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>AS MANY TIMES AS I NEED UNTIL IT STOPS HURTING</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>F/F</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Graphic Depictions Of Violence</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Now rated M for Shadow Weaver being Shadow Weaver</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>i.e. a child torturing MONSTER</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora's lack of chill makes its first appearence</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra and Adora have a mutual protective streak and it causes PROBLEMS</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Chapter two has hurt/comfort like wow</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Unsubtle racists getting their comeuppance</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Man all of these kids have steel in their spines and snark in their hearts</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Oh crap the hurt/comfort came back for the finale</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Found family for the win</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Kyle/Rogelio (She-Ra) (side)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Kyle (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Lonnie (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Rogelio (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>"NOT A STANDALONE FIC"</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Bag>
      </dc:subject>
      <dc:publisher>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Archive of Our Own</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Bag>
      </dc:publisher>
      <dc:date>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>2019-11-13T21:00:00-03:00</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:date>
      <dc:language>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>en</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Bag>
